00:04:41.580 --> 00:04:42.810
Companies know this.

00:04:42.810 --> 00:04:45.090
In recent years, they've
taken steps to provide

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:48.960
what Chen calls "pastoral
and spiritual care" at work,

00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:51.030
from weekly meditation sessions,

00:04:51.030 --> 00:04:54.480
to self-fulfillment workshops,
to team building exercises.

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:56.490
Companies are offering
many of the trappings

00:04:56.490 --> 00:04:58.560
once associated with spiritual life,

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:00.780
all in the name of
boosting our productivity.

00:05:00.780 --> 00:05:03.660
So was the secular religiousafication

00:05:03.660 --> 00:05:05.490
of the American workplace inevitable?

00:05:05.490 --> 00:05:06.690
Arguably not.

00:05:06.690 --> 00:05:09.067
As social researcher, David Frayne writes,

00:05:09.067 --> 00:05:12.450
"If work is indeed a central
source of sociality, rights,

00:05:12.450 --> 00:05:13.800
status and belonging,

00:05:13.800 --> 00:05:16.680
this situation is a social
and historical construction,

00:05:16.680 --> 00:05:19.230
and not a fixed feature
of some natural order.

00:05:19.230 --> 00:05:21.570
So where does our fixation on our work

00:05:21.570 --> 00:05:23.430
and our productivity really come from?

